# 🔹 1500-Word Informative Learning — Part 3

We've already established the central idea:

> **The soldier is not the only person who serves.**

Today, let's go deeper into what the seven stories can teach us about **courage, relationships, responsibility, resilience, leadership and legacy.**

The seven stories are:

1. **The Nation Cried With Her** — Lt Nitika Kaul & Major Vibhuti S. Dhoundiyal
2. **An Eternal Love Story** — Trupti Nair & Major Shashidharan Vijay Nair
3. **Never Give Up** — Major Priya Semwal & Naik Amit Sharma
4. **The Last Gift** — Sujata & Major Satish Dahiya
5. **Two Bodies, One Soul** — Sarika Gulati & Lt Col Rajesh Gulati
6. **An Empowered Woman** — Jaya Mahto & Lance Naik Raj Kumar Mahto
7. **The Kargil Love Story** — Soumya Nagappa & Captain Naveen Nagappa ([Scribd][2])

The author, Swapnil Pandey, is herself an Army wife, and the publisher explains that her experience living among military families motivated her to document the struggles and lives of these families. ([Penguin Random House India][1])

