# 🧠 12. What This Teaches You About Mental Toughness

You've already read **Can't Hurt Me**.

David Goggins emphasizes pushing through physical and psychological limits.

This book provides a different perspective.

### Goggins-style toughness:

**"I will endure the challenge."**

### The Force Behind the Forces:

**"I will continue living responsibly despite what life has taken from me."**

Both are resilience.

But they operate in different environments.

This teaches you that mental toughness isn't one single personality type.

There are **different forms of strength**.

---

# 🔥 13. The Importance of Community

No person handles extreme circumstances entirely alone.

Military families often have:

* Fellow officers
* Regimental families
* Friends
* Parents
* Children
* Communities
* Institutions

That creates a support network.

And this gives us another lesson:

> **Don't try to be strong alone when support is available.**

Asking for help isn't weakness.

Sometimes it is intelligent resource management.

---

# 🧠 14. Gratitude Through Perspective

This book can change how you look at ordinary life.

A normal morning.

Family around you.

Someone calling you.

A friend asking how you're doing.

A peaceful commute.

These things can feel ordinary until you realize that **ordinary life itself is something many people sacrifice to protect.**

The point isn't to live in fear.

It's to develop gratitude.

### Gratitude isn't:

"Everything is perfect."

It's:

> **"I recognize the value of what I currently have."**

